{
  "description": "Answers the Go server must give exactly as the TypeScript deployment does (ADR-0059 step 3, varlatchd-core decision 4). go/server/httpserver/parity_test.go and services/varlatchd/test/go-parity.test.ts both run every case, the TypeScript one against buildApp and Hono's own getPath, from raw request targets. pathVectors: the path varlatchd's router (Hono) routes a raw request target on, after the WHATWG URL parser and decodeURI. nginxVectors: the URI the dashboard's nginx selects a location with ($uri), as nginx 1.29 (the dashboard image's) gave it for each raw target: escapes decoded first, then dot segments resolved and slashes merged. routes: requests and their answers; expect is text (plain-text body), code (the JSON error envelope's code), json (a JSON answer that is not an error), meta (the /v1/meta document) or dashboard (the dashboard's nginx serves its app and never forwards the request to varlatchd, which Go reproduces; the TypeScript side decides forwarding from apps/web/nginx.conf's own locations); a HEAD answer is compared by status and Content-Type only. credential is none, basic (not a bearer), valid (a live CLI credential), browser (a dashboard bearer of a session), invalid (no such credential), revoked, expired, or agent-run (an Agent Run's read-only credential). forwardedFor: X-Forwarded-For sent as several header lines. requestWindow: the 601st request of a window, with the clock held still. body, when present, is sent as written, with Content-Type application/json; bodySize sends a JSON object of exactly that many bytes instead ({\"pad\":\"aaa...\"}); chunked sends the body without a Content-Length (Transfer-Encoding: chunked). Each case runs against a fresh installation. Both servers run with the public URL http://127.0.0.1:8686, so device sign-in is available. transportBodies: requests sent over a real connection (app.request cannot give a GET a body): a body of size bytes, framed chunked or with a Content-Length, and the status. The Node adapter (@hono/node-server) passes GET, HEAD and TRACE on without their body, so the body limit never sees one; every other method's body is limited.",
